      "part": "problem",
      "original_record": "before",
      "value": "Let $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ -5 & k\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],$ where $k$ is a constant such that $k\\ne 1.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $det(A)\\ne 0$\n\nII. $Ax=0$ has no solution\n\nIII. The lines $5x-y=-1$ and $-5x+ky=0$ intersect exactly at one point",
